ExternalRef: SECURITY cpe23Type cpe:2.3:a:espressif:esp-idf:5.5.5:*:*:*:*:*:*:*
ExternalRef: SECURITY cpe23Type cpe:2.3:h:espressif:esp32:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*
ExternalRef: SECURITY cpe23Type cpe:2.3:o:espressif:esp32_firmware:5.5.5:*:*:*:*:*:*:*
ExternalRef: SECURITY cpe23Type cpe:2.3:o:espressif:esp32_firmware:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*
PackageComment: <text>
# The cve-exclude-list list contains CVEs, which were already evaluated and the package is not vulnerable.
cve-exclude-list:
-   cve: CVE-2026-81507
    reason: Out-of-bounds read in the BlueDroid L2CAP configuration option parsing
        (components/bt/host/bluedroid/stack/l2cap/l2c_main.c and l2c_utils.c). Fixed
        in 5.2.8, 5.3.6, 5.5.5, 6.0.3 and 6.1-rc1. release/v5.4 has the fix (5731c63ece12),
        so the next 5.4 release, 5.4.5, has it too. The v6.1-beta1 pre-release also
        reports 6.1.0, but does not have the fix. https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/security/advisories/GHSA-v335-fxwc-rc44
-   cve: CVE-2025-27840
    reason: A security issue was reported concerning undocumented HCI commands in
        ESP32 Bluetooth controller. Espressif had earlier clarified that these vendor
        HCI commands are primarily used for debugging purposes and pose no real, known
        security threat. Technical details were shared in this https://developer.espressif.com/blog/2025/03/esp32-bluetooth-clearing-the-air/
</text>

