-   cve: CVE-2020-22283
    reason: 'ICMPv6 out-of-bounds read (savannah #58553) in icmp6_send_response_with_addrs_and_netif().
        Fixed upstream by commits 489405839ae0 and 488d4ad2460c (lwIP 2.1.3/2.2.0),
        further hardened by 2bf8fcd7c240; all present as ancestors in the vendored
        esp-lwip fork. NVD''s CPE has no fixed-version boundary ("git head"), causing
        the version match.'
-   cve: CVE-2026-87121
    reason: Out-of-bounds write into client->rx_buffer in mqtt_parse_incoming() of
        the lwIP MQTT client application (src/apps/mqtt/mqtt.c), fixed upstream by
        68b2c1191886 (ICSA-26-265-01). ESP-IDF does not build src/apps/mqtt/mqtt.c.
        Its MQTT client is the separate ESP-MQTT component.
-   cve: CVE-2026-15340
    reason: Overflow of tx_buf in smtp_prepare_auth_or_mail() of the lwIP SMTP client
        application (src/apps/smtp/smtp.c) when a server sends an AUTH line longer
        than SMTP_TX_BUF_LEN, fixed upstream by 614420f82c87 (ICSA-26-279-02). The
        advisory lists 2.2.1, but 2.1.3 and 2.2.0 have the same code. ESP-IDF does
        not build src/apps/smtp/smtp.c.
-   cve: CVE-2026-91018
    reason: Double free of the input pbuf in lowpan6_input() of the lwIP 6LoWPAN netif
        (src/netif/lowpan6.c) when decompression of a FRAG1 fragment fails, fixed
        upstream by f873b6295933 (ICSA-26-265-02). ESP-IDF does not build src/netif/lowpan6.c
        or src/netif/lowpan6_common.c. Thread support uses the 6LoWPAN layer of OpenThread.
</text>

